      "title": "Technical Performance Metrics",
      "content": "Benchmark data shows that a single agent host can handle 2,400 requests per second (req/s) at 200 concurrent requests, achieving a 24× speedup compared to a baseline of 100 req/s.  CPU utilization remains below 70% under this load, indicating headroom for additional traffic.  When scaling to 10 hosts, throughput scales linearly to 24,000 req/s, while per‑host CPU utilization stays within the 60–70% range.  Memory usage per host averages 4 GB, with peak usage at 4.5 GB during burst periods.  Latency measurements indicate an average end‑to‑end response time of 120 ms at 200 concurrent requests, rising to 150 ms when the system is saturated.  These metrics provide a quantitative basis for sizing the agent host fleet to meet service level objectives (SLOs) for throughput and latency.",
